# Clean Code & Clean Architecture

Applies to every file added or changed in this project.

## Layers

- `scripts/domain/`, `src/*` domains: pure business rules, no framework or I/O imports.
- Adapters (UI, HTTP, OneSignal, storage) live at the edges: `src/account-ui/`, `scripts/adapters/`, `scripts/*.mjs`.
- Dependencies point inward only: adapters → use cases/domain, never the reverse.
- Keep each module free of more than one reason to change; split files that mix UI, state and I/O.

## Naming & signatures

- Descriptive names over abbreviations; functions named for what they return/do.
- Small functions with a single level of abstraction; early returns instead of deep nesting.
- Plain data in, plain data out: prefer pure functions (as `push-state.js` does) over functions that read globals.
- No boolean trap: take named options (`{ deviceEnabled, accountEnabled }`) and return explicit flags.
- Inject collaborators as parameters or via a thin factory; no module-level singletons inside domain code.

## Errors & side effects

- Throw typed errors at the boundary, translate to user-facing messages in one place (see `pushFailureMessage`).
- Side effects (network, DOM, notifications) are confined to adapter functions; never inside domain logic.
- Never swallow errors silently: log with context and surface a recoverable message.

## Quality bar

- Keep functions readable without comments; comments only for the non-obvious "why".
- No dead code, no commented-out blocks, no speculative abstractions.
- Every change ships with tests in `tests/*.test.mjs` (`node --test`); update existing tests when behavior changes.
- Run `npm run check` (typecheck + tests) before considering work done.
